    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "\"This CD ROM contains a brief review of the coalbed methane potential of Hungary and discussion of proximate and desorption analyses of selected coal beds.  This report is a result of cooperation between the Minerals Management Division of the Hungarian Geological Survey, the U.S. Bureau of Mines, and the U.S. Geological Survey under the auspices of the U.S.-Hungarian Science and Technology Joint Fund.  During studies of the coal resources of Hungary, the potential for recovery and utilization of coalbed gas was recognized and this preliminary study was initiated. Informal cooperation between personnel of the U.S. Geological Survey and the Hungarian Geological Survey has resulted in this report.\"",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
